  "schema": "ancora.parity.scenario.v1",
  "id": "s06-breakdown-options",
  "title": "Subject breakdown options (desglose, D4): the defaults, no order with the same day, Q-04, and a minimum of two days, each in its own specialty",
  "notes": [
    "Issue #70, D4 (legacy-parity-inventory.md PAR-031..035, Q-04, Q-24; SQL case 135). Four specialties share the plan and nothing else: each has its own period (5 days x 3 slots), cohort, group, subject with three templates (orders 1-3), teacher and room. The triggers pair every subject with every period (16 breakdowns). Separate periods keep the period-wide metrics of each run to its own specialty, so the workspace path and the oracles count the same placements.",
    "Legacy side: the breakdown rows come from the triggers; each edit opens the subject's breakdown browser (get_browser_DesgloseDetalles), the form (get_form_edit_desglose) and posts set_Desglose with the fields of the JS client (day counts as text, checkboxes as 1/0). Drupal side: the breakdown entities kept by BreakdownMaintainer, edited through the Entity API as the user.",
    "Subject SD is saved with the defaults (1, 5, respect order, no same day): one template per day. SO: order not respected, same day allowed: the three templates share day 1. SQ: order not respected, same day not allowed: only the first template is placed (Q-04). SM: minimum 2 days: the first template starts on day 2, the second on day 4, the third has no day left (Q-24).",
    "Observed on both sides (placement digests equal): SD 1/1, 2/1, 3/1 (day/slot); SO 1/1, 1/2, 1/3; SQ 1/1 only; SM 2/1, 4/1.",
    "The characterization steps (legacy only, after the comparison) record what set_Desglose does with values the form accepts as text, and that it updates another user's breakdown."
  ],
